91
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:10,120
dividing it into a capitalist West and a communist East. Like Europe,  

92
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:16,400
Germany was also divided into two parts. Horst Fischer decided to stay in Germany.  

93
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:22,720
This and continue working as a doctor. To hide his Nazi past, he removed his group tattoo.  

94
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:29,440
SS sanguine. He married, had four children, and lived the life of a middle-class citizen.

95
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:34,880
In April 1960, the Central Office for the Investigation of National Socialist Crimes  

96
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:40,760
in Ludwigsburg, West Germany, issued an arrest warrant for Horst Fischer,  

97
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:47,920
but was unable to locate him. It was not until April 1964 that the Ministry of State Security  

98
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:54,640
of East Germany, known as the Stasi, became aware of Fischer. Surprisingly,  

99
00:09:54,640 --> 00:10:00,120
It was not his Nazi past that initially caught his attention, but his contacts in  

100
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:05,080
West Germany. Fischer aroused suspicion after crossing the border.  

101
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:10,320
towards West Germany and make negative comments about the Eastern part. Then,  

102
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:14,200
The Stasi contacted West German officials,  

103
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:19,240
who provided them with evidence of Fischer's wartime crimes.

104
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:25,920
In June 1965, Fischer was arrested and remanded in custody. The Stasi  

105
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:31,600
He carefully planned the operation, fearing that he might flee to the West or take off his  

106
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:36,200
life if he discovered the investigation. The arrest took place shortly before  

107
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:41,920
eight in the morning, when three Stasi agents, disguised as traffic police,  

108
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:46,640
They showed up at Fischer's office under the pretext of investigating an accident.  

109
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:52,560
traffic incident involving a Mercedes. Fischer, owner of a Mercedes 190,  

110
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:56,680
He was taken to the garage, where he was arrested and taken to prison.

111
00:10:56,680 --> 00:11:03,280
The secrecy of the operation was crucial, as the Stasi feared losing their “valuable capture.” With the  

112
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:08,480
High-profile Auschwitz trials underway in Frankfurt am Main, West Germany,  

113
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:14,080
